{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-27686b5b-c94e-4749-936b-dcc7208cfc17","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0174Xwot7WSJBt7qYW2mzcd4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L1-053_gaussian_topk_sparse_activation/candidates.jsonl","content":"{\"id\": \"c001\", \"parent\": null, \"stage\": \"feedback\", \"source_sha256\": \"c1b601721d3b0af25748871b13835d30648f21a264714c923126366892c1671b\", \"design\": \"A: one program per row; BLOCK_H=next_pow2(H); in-register f32 two-pass mean+population var (divisor H); host _ndtri scalar Z; bf16 in -> f32 compute -> bf16 out; 1 read + 1 write\", \"config\": {\"BLOCK_H\": \"next_pow2(H)\", \"num_warps\": \"16 if H>=12288 else 8\", \"num_stages\": 2, \"grid\": \"(M,)\"}, \"hypothesis\": \"Fused single-read/single-write bf16 kernel with f32 two-pass stats and host-precomputed _ndtri Z is correct within atol=1e-5/rtol=0.05 and yields a large multi-x speedup over the multi-kernel f32 reference (H1: ~5-8x traffic cut, bandwidth-bound).\", \"static_validation\": {\"dtype_bf16_out\": true, \"shape_preserved\": true, \"stats_f32\": true, \"divisor_H\": true, \"two_pass_var\": true, \"ndtri_exact\": true, \"masked_lanes_where_before_square\": true, \"masked_store\": true, \"early_exit_0\": true, \"int64_row_offset\": true}, \"results\": [{\"uuid\": \"75640ea8-8bb2-546f-b44d-c8d51baee3e4\", \"wl\": 1, \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 16, \"seq_len\": 1163, \"intermediate_size\": 8192}, \"sparsity\": 0.1, \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 12.20269090034043, \"ref_ms\": 4.310326, \"sol_ms\": 0.3532275, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.16689300537109375}, {\"uuid\": \"30b3bded-7830-54c5-a242-75faeae6e052\", \"wl\": 2, \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 2, \"seq_len\": 293, \"intermediate_size\": 12288}, \"sparsity\": 0.3, \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 35.81067488643738, \"ref_ms\": 0.882948, \"sol_ms\": 0.024656, \"max_abs\": 0.00390625, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"151250c8-7c37-56d8-9d87-6edc9f5fd531\", \"wl\": 3, \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 1, \"seq_len\": 512, \"intermediate_size\": 12288}, \"sparsity\": 0.2, \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 40.00232641374373, \"ref_ms\": 0.894132, \"sol_ms\": 0.022352, \"max_abs\": 0.0078125, \"max_rel\": 0.007751937955617905}, {\"uuid\": \"eb88804d-33eb-5840-93b8-235b7f88961a\", \"wl\": 4, \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 1, \"seq_len\": 8192, \"intermediate_size\": 4096}, \"sparsity\": 0.3, \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 19.447495726184847, \"ref_ms\": 1.60401, \"sol_ms\": 0.082479, \"max_abs\": 0.015625, \"max_rel\": 0.011920928955078125}, {\"uuid\": \"75e273d1-070a-5864-a5e2-11f455340620\", \"wl\": 5, \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 4, \"seq_len\": 541, \"intermediate_size\": 8192}, \"sparsity\": 0.3, \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 25.16630183250985, \"ref_ms\": 1.207152, \"sol_ms\": 0.047967, \"max_abs\": 0.0078125, \"max_rel\": 0.009900989942252636}], \"all_pass\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 24.34710284566207, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 26.525897951843245, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"best_after\": \"c001\", \"cumulative_evals\": 1, \"skills_used\": [], \"notes\": \"Correctness anchor / baseline. 5/5 PASSED, geomean 24.35x. WL1 (H=8192, largest, dominates weight) is the lowest speedup at 12.2x and the main remaining lever; its max_rel 0.167 is comfortably within the 99% matched-ratio tolerance. WL4 (H=4096) 19.4x next lowest. H=12288 rows (WL2/WL3) already ~36-40x -> no visible design-A register-spill penalty at num_warps=16. Next: tune num_warps/num_stages branching from c001, focusing on WL1.\"}\n{\"id\": \"c002\", \"parent\": \"c001\", \"stage\": \"feedback\", \"source_sha256\": \"53cab36e690c13a37a1b30d9847b4ac2c7c0273ee7b72cadfaf90d10e12192b2\", \"design\": \"A (same kernel as c001); single knob changed: uniform num_warps=16 for all H (raise the H<=8192 path from 8 -> 16).\", \"config\": {\"BLOCK_H\": \"next_pow2(H)\", \"num_warps\": 16, \"num_stages\": 2, \"grid\": \"(M,)\"}, \"hypothesis\": \"H3/ILP lever: raising num_warps from 8 to 16 on the H<=8192 path halves per-thread element count (H=8192: 32->16 elems/thread) and increases parallel loads in flight, lifting WL1/WL4/WL5 without hurting the already-fast H=12288 path.\", \"static_validation\": {\"dtype_bf16_out\": true, \"shape_preserved\": true, \"stats_f32\": true, \"divisor_H\": true, \"two_pass_var\": true, \"ndtri_exact\": true, \"masked_lanes_where_before_square\": true, \"masked_store\": true, \"early_exit_0\": true, \"int64_row_offset\": true, \"diff_vs_parent\": \"num_warps 8->16 for H<8192 only\"}, \"results\": [{\"uuid\": \"75640ea8-8bb2-546f-b44d-c8d51baee3e4\", \"wl\": 1, \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 16, \"seq_len\": 1163, \"intermediate_size\": 8192}, \"sparsity\": 0.1, \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 12.230407999387108, \"ref_ms\": 4.310326, \"sol_ms\": 0.352427, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.16689300537109375}, {\"uuid\": \"30b3bded-7830-54c5-a242-75faeae6e052\", \"wl\": 2, \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 2, \"seq_len\": 293, \"intermediate_size\": 12288}, \"sparsity\": 0.3, \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 37.26226498702285, \"ref_ms\": 0.882948, \"sol_ms\": 0.0236955, \"max_abs\": 0.00390625, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"151250c8-7c37-56d8-9d87-6edc9f5fd531\", \"wl\": 3, \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 1, \"seq_len\": 512, \"intermediate_size\": 12288}, \"sparsity\": 0.2, \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 42.49777798902064, \"ref_ms\": 0.894132, \"sol_ms\": 0.0210395, \"max_abs\": 0.0078125, \"max_rel\": 0.007751937955617905}, {\"uuid\": \"eb88804d-33eb-5840-93b8-235b7f88961a\", \"wl\": 4, \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 1, \"seq_len\": 8192, \"intermediate_size\": 4096}, \"sparsity\": 0.3, \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 19.157619405926404, \"ref_ms\": 1.60401, \"sol_ms\": 0.083727, \"max_abs\": 0.015625, \"max_rel\": 0.011920928955078125}, {\"uuid\": \"75e273d1-070a-5864-a5e2-11f455340620\", \"wl\": 5, \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 4, \"seq_len\": 541, \"intermediate_size\": 8192}, \"sparsity\": 0.3, \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 25.94519311367593, \"ref_ms\": 1.207152, \"sol_ms\": 0.046527, \"max_abs\": 0.0078125, \"max_rel\": 0.009900989942252636}], \"all_pass\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 24.928432643672647, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 27.41865269900659, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"best_after\": \"c002\", \"cumulative_evals\": 2, \"skills_used\": [], \"notes\": \"5/5 PASSED, geomean 24.93x (+2.4% over c001 24.35x). num_warps=16 uniform helped H=12288 (WL2 35.81->37.26, WL3 40.00->42.50) and WL5 (25.17->25.95); WL1 essentially flat (12.20->12.23, sol_ms 0.3532->0.3524); WL4 slightly DOWN (19.45->19.16, sol_ms 0.0825->0.0837). Correctness margins identical to c001. Accept as new best. Key insight: WL1 (M=18608 x H=8192, sol_ms 0.352 ms, 12.2x) is NOT moving with warps -> it is likely memory-bandwidth bound already, not ILP-bound; the fused kernel is near roofline for WL1. WL4 regressed slightly at warps=16 (fewer rows/SM residency at H=4096). Next lever candidates: (a) num_stages sweep to pipeline loads; (b) rows-per-program for small-H (WL4) to restore its warps=8-like residency; but WL1 (dominant) may be at roofline, capping further geomean gains.\"}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48433,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee48aae6-2689-4135-9623-eaa4a8110b83","uuid":"27717a71-10ca-40d6-8890-0964fd2fb52c","timestamp":"2026-09-16T17:51:49.450Z"}
